WEBVTT

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:03.462 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
TerraScope helps planners
choose where to investigate.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.358 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
Imagine a team in Madhya Pradesh

00:00:05.358 --> 00:00:08.740 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
looking to store floodwater
upstream of a village.

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.939 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
We search near Seondha
on the Sindh River.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.204 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
TerraScope loads terrain,
buildings and water,

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:19.144 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
then downloads September 2024 rainfall
and nearby river-flow history.

00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:22.060 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
The terrain screen finds
low spots near Seondha.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.402 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
Select one to inspect its shape.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:25.767 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
The card shows its footprint

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:29.798 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
and a terrain-based volume
estimate up to the spill rim.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.427 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
Field measurements are needed
to establish usable storage.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.268 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
The cross-section shows the dip.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.630 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
I built TerraScope with an AI agent
and published it with Embarko.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:43.676 line:73% position:46% size:80% align:center
TerraScope. From a planning
question to a place worth surveying.
